{"event_type":"review","id":"2c1cb180df975b985a7c87a16a97206974afc86b3ddd5a40a1e44cef528f0af3","occurred_at":"2026-11-12T02:42:53Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/26b288b913f6cdfcfc24d6fdaf5c92baf81a1a9d63259530eb307155072ef8f4","sha256":"26b288b913f6cdfcfc24d6fdaf5c92baf81a1a9d63259530eb307155072ef8f4"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ee57816eff5ed3ce35e735e6b5250d9f94643b0347d1b72e05569f4414f3d879","sha256":"ee57816eff5ed3ce35e735e6b5250d9f94643b0347d1b72e05569f4414f3d879"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d4f2d9dd5f043bfa13d548661e8230478a479c07c03bcf84128cdcb589b1ed87","sha256":"d4f2d9dd5f043bfa13d548661e8230478a479c07c03bcf84128cdcb589b1ed87"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f4b038fa128addbdd580d314a7f9d3aca220502ee798903f63cc666885941a10","sha256":"f4b038fa128addbdd580d314a7f9d3aca220502ee798903f63cc666885941a10"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/33e9cde4e3338f2552b56bc9277186fe9c177699727cb5985228bb7bcc8607f2","sha256":"33e9cde4e3338f2552b56bc9277186fe9c177699727cb5985228bb7bcc8607f2"}],"attempt_id":"a3156fb975e287e710379d0a429196915570dd633368a563d5e75d734df7efa8:0:1","base":"ab4057f495f52b84c126fc23a145bff89238d84a","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"78ac730836f213d12ea27467601963efee3d8398","body":"**Compare the second record with the saved first record.**\n\n`record` still refers to the queue entry. If the second `prepare_current_job` call changes that entry in place, `record_after == record` remains true. The oracle then reports an unchanged record when the record changed. Compare `record_after` with `record_bytes`, which Line 396 captures before the second call.   \n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed change</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                \"idempotent_record_unchanged\": record_after == record,\n+                \"idempotent_record_unchanged\": _dump(record_after) == record_bytes,\n```\n</details>","id":"6be8691e14f51a517b1998960569beef4c6ac380e0d59b3c6d184f0ad045f356","intervals":[[426,426]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_prepare_vectors.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Compare the second record with the saved first record."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"78ac730836f213d12ea27467601963efee3d8398","body":"**Keep `handoff_calls` at the first-call count.**\n\nLine 449 already sets `handoff_calls` to `first_handoff`. Line 457 then overwrites it with the total `inbox.handoff.call_count`, which includes the second call. The second call replays the handoff, so the recorded value counts that replay. `handoff_args` (line 450) still holds only first-call arguments, so the record now disagrees with itself. The sibling case at lines 607-615 records `handoff_calls` as the first-call count and derives `idempotent_handoff_calls` from the remainder.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n             }\n-            if canonical is not None:\n-                expected[\"handoff_calls\"] = inbox.handoff.call_count\n             if spec.get(\"select_on_prepared\"):\n```\n\n</details>","id":"5b4cee7eda1d46aed0bcdb259fcd2f2785f45f940988a26602e133ee3228edb0","intervals":[[457,457]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_prepare_vectors.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep `handoffcalls` at the first-call count."}],"head":"f1612d4797a33062030015ffadee7b64af1bcd99","head_tree":"fd9b086373c60203765fe780f899178a146a7825","input_scope":[{"blob":"cd716fe062985452a347183ecb6d5898df076e2a","intervals":[[1,1488]],"path":"apps/crq-python/finding_inbox_vector_emit_b1.py"},{"blob":"78ac730836f213d12ea27467601963efee3d8398","intervals":[[1,1288]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_prepare_vectors.py"},{"blob":"57c90edf9